00:14:48.480 --> 00:14:55.280
going come or that script is read by the right&nbsp;
agent or the right assistant to an actor and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:55.280 --> 00:15:00.480
I mean there's always the lottery I mean people&nbsp;
win the lottery that's true I think the odds are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:00.480 --> 00:15:06.320
about the same but I think you need to if you're&nbsp;
not DIY and you need people and you need a staff&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:06.320 --> 00:15:11.680
then what I think you need to do is find other&nbsp;
people that are needing a staff but one of them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:11.680 --> 00:15:16.800
has a camera and one of them is an actor and one&nbsp;
of them may be an editor and work together we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:16.800 --> 00:15:21.280
talked earlier about people working together and&nbsp;
building something special and building building a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:21.280 --> 00:15:26.560
team everybody having a common goal to get to the&nbsp;
next level and that's what I tell a lot of writers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:26.560 --> 00:15:31.120
I said the cool thing about being a writer is&nbsp;
you don't need anybody to tell you to go to work&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:31.120 --> 00:15:38.080
you you really have the only job in this industry&nbsp;
that you you may not get paid yet or at all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:38.080 --> 00:15:43.120
but nobody can tell you you can't work right now&nbsp;
you have the ability to roll out of bed turn on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:43.120 --> 00:15:47.680
a light at two in the morning and write and that's&nbsp;
a beautiful thing because an actor is not going to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:47.680 --> 00:15:52.240
be able to get in front of a camera and tap dance&nbsp;
unless there's a script director doesn't have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:52.240 --> 00:15:55.760
anything to direct unless there's a script there's&nbsp;
nothing to produce without a script the writers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:55.760 --> 00:16:02.320
are essential I mean it's so important it's an&nbsp;
incredible position to be in if you're not able to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:02.320 --> 00:16:07.520
be a writer producer director editor or filmmaker&nbsp;
and all your focus is on writing then you need to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:07.520 --> 00:16:14.240
get out more and you need to find people of like&nbsp;
mind that have those skill sets or the materials&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:14.240 --> 00:16:19.760
to get your products seen it's just it's not going&nbsp;
to sitting in a pdf on an external hard drive or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:20.800 --> 00:16:25.040
somewhere on your computer is not going&nbsp;
to get it made it's about getting it with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:25.040 --> 00:16:29.200
people and I'm very big a lot of people like&nbsp;
to talk about pitch decks and proof of concept&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:30.160 --> 00:16:34.800
some of the most impressive things I've seen&nbsp;
are when people go out and shoot a scene or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:34.800 --> 00:16:39.840
two or three to me that's a real pitch deck&nbsp;
that's a proof of concept I don't want to see&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:40.480 --> 00:16:46.800
papers and comps and actors you're never going&nbsp;
to acquire on your proof of your pitch deck I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:46.800 --> 00:16:53.520
want to see you go out and shoot a scene for&nbsp;
your film with comparable qualified people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:54.400 --> 00:16:59.120
and people that are passionate about&nbsp;
it and I think some of those true&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:59.120 --> 00:17:02.640
pocs [proof of concept] that I've seen they&nbsp;
knock me out of my seat I can't believe what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:02.640 --> 00:17:17.840
people are putting together these days and I&nbsp;
mean for nothing no money there's no excuse.

